{"tag":"section","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae886-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"11373"},"text":"§ 11373.","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Allocation and distribution of assistance","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"subsection","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae887-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/a"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"a"},"text":"(a)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" In general","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"The Secretary shall allocate assistance under this part to metropolitan cities, urban counties, and States (for distribution to local governments and private nonprofit organizations in the States) in a manner that ensures that the percentage of the total amount available under this part for any fiscal year that is allocated to any State, metropolitan city, or urban county is equal to the percentage of the total amount available for ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/usc/t42/s5306"},"text":"section 5306 of this title","children":[],"tail":" for such prior fiscal year that is allocated to such State, metropolitan city, or urban county."}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"subsection","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae888-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/b"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"b"},"text":"(b)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Minimum allocation requirement","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"If, under the allocation provisions applicable under this part, any metropolitan city or urban county would receive a grant of less than 0.05 percent of the amounts appropriated under ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/usc/t42/s11364"},"text":"section 11364 of this title","children":[],"tail":" and made available to carry out this part for any fiscal year, such amount shall instead be reallocated to the State, except that any city that is located in a State that does not have counties as local governments, that has a population greater than 40,000 but less than 50,000 as used in determining the fiscal year 1987 community development block grant program allocation, and that was allocated in excess of $1,000,000 in community development block grant funds in fiscal year 1987, shall receive directly the amount allocated to such city under subsection (a)."}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"subsection","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae889-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/c"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"c"},"text":"(c)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Distributions to nonprofit organizations, public housing agencies, and local redevelopment authorities","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"Any local government receiving assistance under this part may distribute all or a portion of such assistance to private nonprofit organizations providing assistance to homeless individuals, to public housing agencies (as defined under ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/usc/t42/s1437a/b/6"},"text":"section 1437a(b)(6) of this title","children":[],"tail":"), or to local redevelopment authorities (as defined under State law). Any State receiving assistance under this part may distribute all or a portion of such assistance to private nonprofit organizations providing assistance to homeless individuals, if the local government for the locality in which the project is located certifies that it approves of the project."}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"subsection","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae88a-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/d"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"d"},"text":"(d)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Reallocation of funds","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"paragraph","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae88b-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/d/1"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"1"},"text":"(1)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" The Secretary shall, not less than once during each fiscal year, reallocate any assistance provided under this part that is unused or returned or that becomes available under subsection (b).","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"paragraph","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae88c-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/d/2"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"2"},"text":"(2)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" If a city or county eligible for a grant under subsection (a) fails to obtain approval of its comprehensive plan during the 90-day period following the date funds authorized by this part first become available for allocation during any fiscal year, the amount that the city or county would have received shall be available to the State in which the city or county is located if the State has obtained approval of its comprehensive plan. Any amounts that cannot be allocated to a State under the preceding sentence shall be reallocated to other States, counties, and cities that demonstrate extraordinary need or large numbers of homeless individuals, as determined by the Secretary.","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"paragraph","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae88d-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/d/3"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"3"},"text":"(3)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" If a State fails to obtain approval of its comprehensive plan during the 90-day period following the date funds authorized by this part first become available for allocation during any fiscal year, the amount that the State would have received shall be reallocated to other States and to cities and counties as applicable, that demonstrate extraordinary need or large numbers of homeless individuals, as determined by the Secretary.","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"subsection","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae88e-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/e"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"e"},"text":"(e)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Allocations to territories","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"In addition to the other allocations required in this section, the Secretary shall (for amounts appropriated after ","children":[{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"1987-07-22"},"text":"July 22, 1987","children":[],"tail":") allocate assistance under this part to the Virgin Islands, Guam, American Samoa, the Northern Mariana Islands, the Trust Territory of the Pacific Islands, and any other territory or possession of the United States, in accordance with an allocation formula established by the Secretary."}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"subsection","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae88f-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"f"},"text":"(f)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Funding cap waiver authority","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"paragraph","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae890-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/1"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"1"},"text":"(1)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" In general","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"Notwithstanding any other provision of law or regulation, a recipient may request a waiver to the expenditure limit established pursuant to ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/usc/t42/s11374/b"},"text":"section 11374(b) of this title","children":[],"tail":" for amounts provided for each of fiscal years 2027 through 2030."}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"paragraph","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae891-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/2"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"2"},"text":"(2)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Waiver request","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"subparagraph","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae892-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/2/A"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"A"},"text":"(A)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" In general","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"chapeau","attrib":{},"text":"A recipient seeking a waiver described in paragraph (1) shall submit to the Secretary a waiver request that includes not more than the following:","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"clause","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae893-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/2/A/i"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"i"},"text":"(i)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" A demonstration of local needs and circumstances that necessitate a waiver.","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"clause","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae894-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/2/A/ii"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"ii"},"text":"(ii)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" A detailed plan for how the recipient intends to use funds.","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"clause","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae895-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/2/A/iii"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"iii"},"text":"(iii)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" A justification for how the proposed use of funds supports the most recent Consolidated Plan submitted by the recipient.","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"clause","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae896-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/2/A/iv"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"iv"},"text":"(iv)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" Any public input solicited under subparagraph (B)(ii).","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"subparagraph","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae897-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/2/B"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"B"},"text":"(B)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Notification","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"chapeau","attrib":{},"text":"Each recipient shall—","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"clause","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae898-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/2/B/i"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"i"},"text":"(i)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" notify all subrecipients and local Continuums of Care that serve the recipient’s geographic area of the availability of waivers under this subsection; and","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"clause","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae899-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/2/B/ii"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"ii"},"text":"(ii)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" prior to the submission of a waiver request under subparagraph (A), solicit public input regarding the potential need for and proposed uses of such waiver.","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"subparagraph","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae89a-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/2/C"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"C"},"text":"(C)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Approval; publication","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"chapeau","attrib":{},"text":"The Secretary shall—","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"clause","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae89b-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/2/C/i"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"i"},"text":"(i)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" make all waiver requests submitted under subparagraph (A) publicly available on the website of the Department of Housing and Urban Development;","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"clause","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae89c-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/2/C/ii"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"ii"},"text":"(ii)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" not later than 60 days after the date on which the Secretary receives a waiver request under subparagraph (A), approve or deny the request; and","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"clause","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae89d-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/2/C/iii"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"iii"},"text":"(iii)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" deny any waiver request submitted under subparagraph (A) by a recipient that relocates or threaten ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"idref":"fn004006"},"text":"1","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"note","attrib":{"type":"footnote","id":"fn004006"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{},"text":"1","children":[],"tail":" So in original. Probably should be “threatens”."}],"tail":" to relocate individuals or their property without providing emergency shelter, rapid rehousing, transitional housing, permanent supportive housing, or other permanent housing options."}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"paragraph","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae89e-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/3"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"3"},"text":"(3)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Revocation","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"subparagraph","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae89f-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/3/A"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"A"},"text":"(A)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" In general","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"A waiver approved under this subsection shall remain in effect for the duration of the period of performance of fiscal year 2027 through 2030 grants, unless the recipient notifies the Secretary in writing that the recipient wishes to revoke the waiver.","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"subparagraph","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae8a0-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/3/B"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"B"},"text":"(B)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Notification","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"chapeau","attrib":{},"text":"If a recipient intends to revoke a waiver under subparagraph (A), the recipient shall—","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"clause","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae8a1-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/3/B/i"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"i"},"text":"(i)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" solicit input from subrecipients regarding the revocation before submitting the revocation; and","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"clause","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae8a2-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/3/B/ii"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"ii"},"text":"(ii)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":" provide subrecipients with a summary of the input and the justification for the revocation in its submittal prior to notifying the Secretary in writing.","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"subparagraph","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae8a3-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/s11373/f/3/C"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"C"},"text":"(C)","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Publication","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"The Secretary shall publish any revocation of a waiver under subparagraph (A) and the justification of the recipient for the waiver on the website of the Department of Housing and Urban Development.","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"sourceCredit","attrib":{"id":"id9c3ae8a4-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc"},"text":"(","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/100/77/tIV/s414"},"text":"Pub. L. 100–77, title IV, § 414","children":[],"tail":", formerly § 413, "},{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"1987-07-22"},"text":"July 22, 1987","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/101/496"},"text":"101 Stat. 496","children":[],"tail":"; "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/100/628/tIV/s421"},"text":"Pub. L. 100–628, title IV, § 421","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"1988-11-07"},"text":"Nov. 7, 1988","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/102/3231"},"text":"102 Stat. 3231","children":[],"tail":"; "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/101/625/tVIII/s832/f/3"},"text":"Pub. L. 101–625, title VIII, § 832(f)(3)","children":[],"tail":"–(5), "},{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"1990-11-28"},"text":"Nov. 28, 1990","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/104/4361"},"text":"104 Stat. 4361","children":[],"tail":"; "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/104/330/tV/s506/a/3"},"text":"Pub. L. 104–330, title V, § 506(a)(3)","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"1996-10-26"},"text":"Oct. 26, 1996","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/110/4044"},"text":"110 Stat. 4044","children":[],"tail":"; renumbered § 414 and amended "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/111/22/dB/tII/s1201/3"},"text":"Pub. L. 111–22, div. B, title II, § 1201(3)","children":[],"tail":", (5), "},{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"2009-05-20"},"text":"May 20, 2009","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/123/1678"},"text":"123 Stat. 1678","children":[],"tail":", 1679; "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/114/94/dG/tLXXIX/s79002"},"text":"Pub. L. 114–94, div. G, title LXXIX, § 79002","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"2015-12-04"},"text":"Dec. 4, 2015","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/129/1792"},"text":"129 Stat. 1792","children":[],"tail":"; "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/114/201/tIV/s402"},"text":"Pub. L. 114–201, title IV, § 402","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"2016-07-29"},"text":"July 29, 2016","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/130/808"},"text":"130 Stat. 808","children":[],"tail":"; "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/119/101/tV/s503"},"text":"Pub. L. 119–101, title V, § 503","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"2026-07-11"},"text":"July 11, 2026","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/140/928"},"text":"140 Stat. 928","children":[],"tail":".)"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"notes","attrib":{"type":"uscNote","id":"id9c3ae8a5-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc"},"text":"\n","children":[{"tag":"note","attrib":{"role":"crossHeading","topic":"editorialNotes","id":"id9c3ae8a6-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"b","attrib":{},"text":"Editorial Notes","children":[],"tail":null}],"tail":null}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"note","attrib":{"topic":"priorProvisions","id":"id9c3ae8a7-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":"Prior Provisions","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"A prior ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/100/77/s414"},"text":"section 414 of Pub. L. 100–77","children":[],"tail":" was classified to "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/usc/t42/s11374"},"text":"section 11374 of this title","children":[],"tail":" prior to renumbering as section 415 and repeal by "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/111/22"},"text":"Pub. L. 111–22","children":[],"tail":"."}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"note","attrib":{"topic":"amendments","id":"id9c3ae8a8-86b3-11f1-9949-c831ab2bbedc"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":"Amendments","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"2026—Subsec. (f). ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/119/101"},"text":"Pub. L. 119–101","children":[],"tail":" added subsec. (f)."}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"2016—Subsec. (c). ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/114/201"},"text":"Pub. L. 114–201","children":[],"tail":", inserted “, public housing agencies, and local redevelopment authorities” after “organizations” in heading and inserted “, to public housing agencies (as defined under "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/usc/t42/s1437a/b/6"},"text":"section 1437a(b)(6) of this title","children":[],"tail":"), or to local redevelopment authorities (as defined under State law)” before period at end of first sentence."}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"2015—Subsec. (d)(1). ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/114/94"},"text":"Pub. L. 114–94","children":[],"tail":" substituted “once” for “twice”."}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"2009—Subsec. (b). ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/111/22/s1201/5"},"text":"Pub. L. 111–22, § 1201(5)","children":[],"tail":", substituted “amounts appropriated under "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/usc/t42/s11364"},"text":"section 11364 of this title","children":[],"tail":" and made available to carry out this part for any” for “amounts appropriated to carry out this part for any”."}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"1996—Subsec. (a). ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/104/330/s506/a/3/A"},"text":"Pub. L. 104–330, § 506(a)(3)(A)","children":[],"tail":", struck out “, and to Indian tribes,” after “in the States)” and “, or for Indian tribes” after “or urban county” in two places."}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"Subsec. (c). ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/104/330/s506/a/3/B"},"text":"Pub. L. 104–330, § 506(a)(3)(B)","children":[],"tail":", struck out “or Indian tribe” after “Any local government”."}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"Subsec. (d)(3). ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/104/330/s506/a/3/C/ii"},"text":"Pub. L. 104–330, § 506(a)(3)(C)(ii)","children":[],"tail":", struck out “, or other Indian tribes,” after “cities and counties”."}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/104/330/s506/a/3/C/i"},"text":"Pub. L. 104–330, § 506(a)(3)(C)(i)","children":[],"tail":", which directed amendment of par. (3) by striking “, or Indian tribe” each place it appeared, was executed by striking “or Indian tribe” after “State” in two places to reflect the probable intent of Congress."}],"tail":"\n